

#### 24.3.3 Divisor Functions

I. Definitions

A. \(\sigma_{n}(n)\) is the sum of the \(k\)-th powers of the divisors of \(n\). Often \(\sigma_{0}(n)\) is denoted by \(d(n)\), and \(\sigma_{1}(n)\) by \(\sigma(n)\).

B. Generating functions

\[\begin{array}{l}\sum\limits_{n=1}^{\infty}\sigma_{k}(n)n^{-s}=\zeta(s)\zeta( s-k)\quad\varnothing\delta>k+1\\ \sum\limits_{n=1}^{\infty}\sigma_{k}(n)x^{s}=\sum\limits_{n=1}^{\infty}\frac{n^ {s}x^{s}}{1-x^{s}}\qquad|z|<1\end{array}\]

C. Closed form

\[\sigma_{k}(n)=\sum\limits_{d\ln}d^{s}=\frac{t}{i!}\frac{p_{1}^{t}a^{t+D}-1}{p_ {1}^{t}-1}\qquad n=p_{1}^{t}p_{2}^{s}\ldots p_{2}^{s}\]

II. Relations

A. Recurrences

\[\sigma_{k}(mn)=\sigma_{k}(m)\sigma_{k}(n)\qquad(m,\,n)=1\]

\[\sigma_{k}(np)=\sigma_{k}(n)\sigma_{k}(p)-p^{k}\sigma_{k}(n/p)\qquad p\text{ prime}\]

III. Asymptotics

\[\frac{1}{n}\sum\limits_{m=1}^{n}\sigma_{0}(m)=\ln n+2\gamma-1+O(n^{-1})\]

(\(\gamma=\)Euler's constant)

